            <ArticleTitle>[Relationship between myocardial contractility and collateral circulation in patients with ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>By analyzing coronary angiograms and ventriculograms of 61 patients with the narrowed lumen of one or several coronary vessels by 90-100%, the dependence of the contractile function of the myocardium on the development of the collateral circulation in the cardiac muscle was studied. The assessment of the segmentary contractility of the left ventricle served as a criterion of the efficiency of the collateral circulation. The segmentary contractility was shown to be dependent on the presence or absence of the collateral circulation and also on the number of damaged vessels. The collateral circulation was also demonstrated to contribute to the maintenance of the contractile function of the myocardium.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
